# Taskboard: the weekly flow, as a 45-second demo for the customer.
@id      taskboard-weekly
@title   Taskboard — the weekly flow
@subtitle See the week, add work, finish it
@budget  45
@assert  warn

cut
  go /#/board
  wait ready

== The board
say One **board** shows every task by stage: to do, doing, done
point #col-todo label="To do" hold=0.9
point #col-doing label="Doing" hold=0.9
point #col-done label="Done" hold=0.9

== Add a task
say Add work in seconds: a **title**, who owns it and when it's due
click button:"+ New task" => expect dialog:"New task" visible
type #task-title "Prepare Q4 demo"
pick #task-who "Ava"
click button:"Create task" => expect "Prepare Q4 demo" visible; expect dialog:"New task" hidden
say The new task lands in **To do**, owned by Ava

== Finish it
say Drag a card to **Done** when it's finished
drag "Customer interview notes" to=#col-done => expect "Customer interview notes" in #col-done visible
zoom #weekly-goal pad=60
say Every finished task counts toward the **weekly goal**
point #weekly-goal label="9 of 12 this week" hold=1.6
unzoom

== The trend
click button:"Reports" => expect heading:"Reports" visible
say **Reports** show the trend week by week, and who has what open
point #chart-done label="Done per week" hold=1.4
shot weekly_chart clip=#chart-done
point #table-people label="Open vs done" hold=1.6
